y to have the artist turn the camera back on its owner.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":1004663,\"title\":\"All the Beauty and the Bloodshed\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cvO51xxtIUHc5w5ZgFsigiFaUaO.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/anw7ONmtm1BrHd1Du0GQ5FoNd6r.jpg\",\"rating\":7.2,\"year\":2022,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"The life of internationally renowned artist and activist Nan Goldin is told through her slideshows, intimate interviews, ground-breaking photography, and rare footage of her personal fight to hold the Sackler family accountable for the overdose crisis.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":451995,\"title\":\"Faces Places\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/1NX6NTj9FiiJwEgRUmEifSzE7Na.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/w4uYP6ebNaLQIjsHcjQhjz3BB2m.jpg\",\"rating\":7.6,\"year\":2017,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Director Agnès Varda and photographer/muralist JR journey through rural France and form an unlikely friendship.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":252511,\"title\":\"The Kingdom of Dreams and Madness\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ice7zuzzwcuKO5SJG7aTqYZC3EI.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/muaflceN4wem4NTHXifCRj8upMh.jpg\",\"rating\":7.6,\"year\":2013,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Follows the behind-the-scenes work of Studio Ghibli, focusing on the notable figures Hayao Miyazaki, Isao Takahata, and Toshio Suzuki.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":413765,\"title\":\"David Lynch: The Art Life\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pgtQceTZKylB2B237t18h2pOXpE.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/9qMP1aquRST8XfJ58EqTMAZ9kA6.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"year\":2017,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"An intimate journey through the formative years of David Lynch's life. From his idyllic upbringing in small town America to the dark streets of Philadelphia, we follow Lynch as he traces the events that have helped to shape one of cinema's most enigmatic directors.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":169607,\"title\":\"Finding Vivian Maier\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yaj9mpHNpns5j4ODP4352PgDWJM.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/ajukqMGU1d5d1Csx0jUGPDsXpFC.jpg\",\"rating\":7.6,\"year\":2014,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Vivian Maier's photos were seemingly destined for obscurity, lost among the clutter of the countless objects she'd collected throughout her life. Instead these images have shaken the world of street photography and irrevocably changed the life of the man who brought them to the public eye. This film brings to life the interesting turns and travails of the improbable saga of John Maloof's discovery of Vivian Maier, unravelling this mysterious tale through her documentary films, photographs, odd collections and personal accounts from the people that knew her. What started as a blog to show her work quickly became a viral sensation in the photography world. Photos destined for the trash heap now line gallery exhibitions, a forthcoming book and this documentary film.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":212063,\"title\":\"Tim's Vermeer\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vEF0f8dktdp4NbUbpi0xSzwUAY8.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/pY6gDWUjRmh785MRVHLgnqM9fV2.jpg\",\"rating\":7.2,\"year\":2013,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Tim Jenison, a Texas based inventor, attempts to solve one of the greatest mysteries in all art: How did Dutch Master Johannes Vermeer manage to paint so photo-realistically 150 years before the invention of photography? Spanning a decade, Jenison's adventure takes him to Holland, on a pilgrimage to the North coast of Yorkshire to meet artista David Hockney, and eventually even to Buckingham Palace. The epic research project Jenison embarques on is as extraordinary as what he discovers.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":664372,\"title\":\"Les vendredis d'Apostrophes\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ewMifK17s1147QoVGF7Xna2rcmA.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/aItcbIKzpoMhMrAWlmU9qqzQvdx.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"year\":2015,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Hours and historical meetings, Pierre Assouline has composed an anthology of the best extracts presented in the form of a primer, which he had commented on by a surprised Bernard Pivot.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":480065,\"title\":\"Basquiat: Rage to Riches\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dIJyTw4kUORZcz318wGFkHOPJhy.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/lw3nj4TsQEAfrhQmFAl1HAyp8dp.jpg\",\"rating\":6,\"year\":2017,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"This film tells Jean-Michel's story through exclusive interviews with his two sisters Lisane and Jeanine, who have never before agreed to be interviewed for a TV documentary. With striking candour, Basquiat's art dealers - including Larry Gagosian, Mary Boone and Bruno Bischofberger - as well as his most intimate friends, lovers and fellow artists, expose the cash, the drugs and the pernicious racism which Basquiat confronted on a daily basis. As historical tableaux, visual diaries of defiance or surfaces covered with hidden meanings, Basquiat's art remains the beating heart of this story.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":667856,\"title\":\"Paris Calligrammes\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ly7T4hwyt6EgdMvLSnhi4zamIvp.jpg\",\"backdrop\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/80ta9vcZMaqWOD0RyIfh7B1QV35.jpg\",\"rating\":5.5,\"year\":2020,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Ulrike Ottinger weaves her personal memories of Parisian bohemianism and the serious social, political and cultural upheavals of the time into a cinematic “figure poem.”\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":1635850,\"title\":\"Paving the Way\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/wDNyaVcGVnQqWUjghkCbWpBKZKB.jpg\",\"backdrop\":null,\"rating\":2,\"year\":2026,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Set against the sweeping landscapes of the Flathead Indian Reservation, the film highlights skateboarding’s power to build community, foster confidence, and challenge stereotypes. More than a skateboarding film, it becomes a vibrant portrait of young  people who get back up every time they fall.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null},{\"id\":1473848,\"title\":\"Quest for Beauty: The Life and Art of William Schickel\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/wnCRNOv0KCk1Wt68KY5wzNziaF7.jpg\",\"backdrop\":null,\"rating\":0,\"year\":2025,\"type\":\"movie\",\"overview\":\"Quest for Beauty is a film documentary on the life and prolific art career of William Schickel who was a prominent 20th century Catholic artist. Schickel had a very prolific art career spanning sixty-plus years; he produced a large body of mostly commissioned work in painting, sculpture, stained glass, and architectural design. He is most well-known for his renovation of the Abbey of Gethsemani in Kentucky, where he worked personally with Thomas Merton. His works can be found in numerous private collections and museums, including the Vatican Museum. The film explores his Quest for Beauty and the challenges he faced, and his vision for the Church and his heart for unity in the Body of Christ.\",\"genres\":[\"Documentary\"],\"daysUntil\":null}],\"videos\":[{\"key\":\"eY6aIUp_5eQ\",\"name\":\"OFFICIAL TRAILER | SUNFLOWERS (2021)\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"daysUntil\":null}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}